.SH "@eslint-community/regexpp"
.PP
\fR\fP \fR\fP \fR\fP \fR\fP

.PP
A regular expression parser for ECMAScript\&.
.SH "💿 Installation"
.PP
.PP
.nf
$ npm install @eslint\-community/regexpp
.fi
.PP

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
require Node@^12\&.0\&.0 || ^14\&.0\&.0 || >=16\&.0\&.0\&.
.PP
.SH "📖 Usage"
.PP
.PP
.nf
import {
    AST,
    RegExpParser,
    RegExpValidator,
    RegExpVisitor,
    parseRegExpLiteral,
    validateRegExpLiteral,
    visitRegExpAST
} from "@eslint\-community/regexpp"
.fi
.PP
.SS "parseRegExpLiteral(source, options?)"
Parse a given regular expression literal then make AST object\&.

.PP
This is equivalent to \fRnew RegExpParser(options)\&.parseLiteral(source)\fP\&.

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBParameters:\fP
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fRsource\fP (\fRstring | RegExp\fP) The source code to parse\&.
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fRoptions?\fP (\fR\fRRegExpParser\&.Options\fP\fP) The options to parse\&.
.PP

.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBReturn:\fP
.IP "  \(bu" 4
The AST of the regular expression\&.
.PP

.PP
.SS "validateRegExpLiteral(source, options?)"
Validate a given regular expression literal\&.

.PP
This is equivalent to \fRnew RegExpValidator(options)\&.validateLiteral(source)\fP\&.

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBParameters:\fP
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fRsource\fP (\fRstring\fP) The source code to validate\&.
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fRoptions?\fP (\fR\fRRegExpValidator\&.Options\fP\fP) The options to validate\&.
.PP

.PP
.SS "visitRegExpAST(ast, handlers)"
Visit each node of a given AST\&.

.PP
This is equivalent to \fRnew RegExpVisitor(handlers)\&.visit(ast)\fP\&.

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBParameters:\fP
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fRast\fP (\fR\fRAST\&.Node\fP\fP) The AST to visit\&.
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fRhandlers\fP (\fR\fRRegExpVisitor\&.Handlers\fP\fP) The callbacks\&.
.PP

